lg:GB-SI-2013-3134-r14-4-q1
    a lgo:Quote ;
    lgo:officialLanguageVersion true ;
    lgo:quoteOf lg:GB-SI-2013-3134-r14-4 ;
    lgo:retrievedOn "2026-11-07"^^xsd:date ;
    lgo:sourceDocument lg:GB-SI-2013-3134-source ;
    lgo:sourceElement "/Legislation/Secondary[1]/Body[1]/Part[2]/Chapter[1]/P1group[8]/P1[1]/P1para[1]/P2[4]" ;
    lgo:sourceUrl "https://www.legislation.gov.uk/uksi/2013/3134/regulation/14"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    lgo:text "(4) If placing an order entails activating a button or a similar function, the trader must ensure that the button or similar function is labelled in an easily legible manner only with the words ‘order with obligation to pay’ or a corresponding unambiguous formulation indicating that placing the order entails an obligation to pay the trader."@en .

